{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/listen","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"listen","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLListen","text":"MXLListen","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLListenV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<listen>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"listen","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLListen","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLListenV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV6listenAA9MXLListenVSgvp","title":"listen"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/listen"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Listening information associated with this note, if any.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLListen":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLListen","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLListen","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The listen and listening types, new in Version 4.0, specify different ways that a score following or machine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"listening application can interact with a performer. The listen type handles interactions that are specific to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a note. If multiple child elements of the same type are present, they should have distinct player and\/or time-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only attributes."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLListen","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLListen","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllisten"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/listen":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Listening information associated with this note, if any."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/listen","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"listen","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLListen","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLListenV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"listen","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/listen"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}